course: dictionary
lesson: 486
title: The small word as
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «As» is one of the smallest words, but it has many jobs. It can show two things are equal, give a reason, show two things happening at the same time, or show a role. The words around it are the clues.
explain: William Wordsworth wrote «I wandered lonely as a cloud»: he compares himself to a cloud. In «as tall as his dad», the two heights are the same. Ask yourself: is something being compared, is it about time, is it a reason, or is it a role?
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. In «as it was raining, we stayed inside», as means because, and the sentence still makes sense. In «as I walked in, the bell rang», as means at the same time.
fact: «As» can mean in the role of: «she works as a nurse».
fact: «As» can show equal amounts: «as tall as his dad»; «twice as many as» means two times as many.
fact: «As» can mean at the same time: «as I walked in, the bell rang».
fact: «As» can mean because: «as it was raining, we stayed inside»; «such as» means for example, as in «streaming services such as Spotify».
exercise: In «She works as a nurse», what does as mean? | Equal to | At the same time | Because | *In the role of
exercise: Which sentence uses as to show two things are equal? | She works as a nurse. | *He is as tall as his dad. | As I walked in, the bell rang. | As it was raining, we stayed inside.
exercise: «As it was raining, we stayed inside.» What does as mean here? | As if | In the role of | *Because | At the same time
test: In «as I walked in, the bell rang», what does as mean? | Equal to | In the role of | *At the same time | Because
test: What does «twice as many as» mean? | Half as many | *Two times as many | As if | Exactly the same place
exam: In «as follows», what does as help the writer do? | Give a reason | Show two things are equal | *Introduce what comes next in a stiff, formal way | Ask a question
